1124:
Signs which did not meet all requirements of this article when enacted, or which do not meet provisions of this article at the time of its amendment, may stay in place until one of the following conditions occurs:
(1) The deterioration of the sign or damage to the sign makes it a hazard;
(2) No conforming principal use or accessory use ground or wall sign shall be permitted to be erected on the same property with an existing nonconforming sign until the nonconforming sign has been removed or made to conform to the provisions of this article;
(3) Upon a change of ownership, the subsequent owner will be granted six months to bring all nonconforming signs into conformance with the White County Sign Regulations.
(Res. No. 2005-27, 10-4-05; Res. No. 2011-05, 1-14-11)
